        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>DORCAS</strong> a female antelope, or gazelle, a pious Christian widow at Joppa whom Peter restored to life (Acts 9:36-41). She was a Hellenistic Jewess, called Tabitha by the Jews and Dorcas by the Greeks.",
