        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>SALAMIS</strong> a city on the south-east coast of Cyprus (Acts 13:5), where Saul and Barnabas, on their first missionary journey, preached the word in one of the Jewish synagogues, of which there seem to have been several in that place. It is now called Famagusta.",
