        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>JULIUS</strong> the centurion of the Augustan cohort, or the emperor’s body-guard, in whose charge Paul was sent prisoner to Rome (Acts 27:1, 3, 43). He entreated Paul “courteously,” showing in many ways a friendly regard for him.",
