        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>CASTOR AND POLLUX</strong> the “Dioscuri”, two heroes of Greek and Roman mythology. Their figures were probably painted or sculptured on the prow of the ship which Luke refers to (Acts 28:11). They were regarded as the tutelary divinities of sailors. They appeared in the heavens as the constellation Gemini.",
