        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>SYRACUSE</strong> a city on the south-east coast of Sicily, where Paul landed and remained three days when on his way to Rome (Acts 28:12). It was distinguished for its magnitude and splendour. It is now a small town of some 13,000 inhabitants.",
